  {
   "n": 14,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • Data Science & Artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>Consider a linked list of length n is implemented using a circular array <em>P</em>[0, <em>n</em> – 1], two variables first and last are used to point the first and last element of the list present in array respectively i.e., first = <em>P</em> and last = (<em>P</em> + <em>x</em>) mod <em>n</em>, where <em>x</em> is the size of linked list.<br />\nConsider the following operations:<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Delete <em>k<sup>th</sup></em> element in linked list.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Reverse the elements of linked list.<br />\nWhich of the following represent the time complexity of above two operations respectively?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "Ο(<em>n</em>), Ο(<em>n</em>)"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "Ο(<em>n</em>), Ο(1)"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "Ο(1), Ο(1)"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "Ο(1), Ο(n)"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>(a)<br />\nOperation 1<br />\n&bull; Search k<sup>th</sup> element in array take &Omicron;(1) time.<br />\n&bull; Delete take &Omicron;(1) time<br />\n&bull; Shift all element to left if space is there &Omicron;(n)<br />\nTotal time = &Omicron;(1) + &Omicron;(1) + &Omicron;(n) = &Omicron;(n)<br />\nOperation 2<br />\n&bull; Reversal of linked list will take &Omicron;(n) time since circular array has to follow the properties of<br />\nlinked list.</p>"
  },
